{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>They do not know.</b> The faculty of knowledge is in the apertures close to the forehead, and understanding is in the middle aperture, which is inside the head." "<b>For He has smeared.</b> Like \"and he shall smear the house\" (Leviticus 14:42); it is a transitive verb, and the agent is HaShem." "<b>Their eyes.</b> Each one, and similarly [the verb is] plural."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:58.970290439Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}